.TH "TUIL" "1" "{release_date}" "Version {version}" "Usage and Commands"
.SH NAME
TUIL - Terminal UI for Lemmy
.SH SYNOPSIS
{synopsis}
.SH DESCRIPTION
{description}
.SH OPTIONS
{options}
.SH CONTROLS
Move the cursor using the arrow keys or vim style movement.
.br
Press \fBup\fR and \fBdown\fR to scroll through posts.
.br
Press \fBright\fR to view the selected post and \fBleft\fR to return.
.br
Press \fB?\fR to open the help screen.
.SH FILES
.TP
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tuil/tuil.cfg
The configuration file can be used to customize default program settings.
.TP
.BR $XDG_DATA_HOME/tuil/token
After you log in to a Lemmy instance, the session token will be stored for
future sessions. Tokens are bound to the instance that issued them.
.TP
.BR $XDG_DATA_HOME/tuil/history.log
This file stores URLs that have been recently opened in order to
visually highlight them as "seen".
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR TUIL_EDITOR
Text editor to use when editing comments and posts. Will fallback to
\fI$EDITOR\fR.
.TP
.BR TUIL_URLVIEWER
Url viewer to use to extract links from comments.  Requires a compatible
program to be installed.
.TP
.BR TUIL_BROWSER
Web browser to use when opening links. Will fallback to \fI$BROWSER\fR.
